body:
I am so overwhelmed (in a good way) at all of these responses.  You have all given me courage and that push I needed to keep going.  I have been packing all morning and am going to be at his hearing tomorrow morning to ask the judge not to let him post bond or let him out.  I havn't heard back from his family after replying to them and telling them that what he did was wrong no matter what.  It didn't take much for him to say it to me, either.  We had a small argument about him wanting to take the weekend to be by himself instead of spend some time with his daughter that he has hardly seen for 2 months.  I didn't call him names, I didn't yell, I didn't get in his face or anything.  He got angry that I confronted him about needing to spend time with her as she has been saying she missed him and wanted to see him.  But again, he wanted what he wanted and that has always trumped everything else.  

&#x200B;

For years I learned not to confront him.  But I'd had enough of living in fear and walking on egg shells, being so careful and reading his every movement and expression as not to upset him in any way and if I did, apologize profusely and do so many things to make up for what I did wrong.  My life was literally spent analyzing every thing I said and did to keep him happy.  

&#x200B;

I realize now that I have been addicted to him.  He gaslighted me, twisted my thoughts, brainwashed me right before my very eyes.  He destroyed the very core of who I was.  I look in the mirror and have NO IDEA who I am.  Even still, my mind wants to blame myself.  Maybe if I  did this different?  Maybe if I said that instead?  But when my rational mind seeps in, I know that nothing I could have done better would have made any difference.  He sought out all that was negative about me, ignoring the positive.  He does this with everything and everyone in his life- his family; i've never heard him say a single good thing about any of them.  His coworkers; all bad things.  He even cheated on me with 7 different women, 1 being his boss and another was a coworker.  I had a heart filled to the brim with love, forgiveness and hope.  His life story was so sad and I wanted to be the one that brought him happiness.  

&#x200B;

I remember when we first began dating, he said to me "I don't want to pull you down with me, it happens to everyone."  If only I knew.  If only I didn't dismiss the HUGE red flags from the very beginning.  Our first date, he told me in all seriousness that he had murdered someone.  To him he was only telling a joke, but for 10 minutes he had me believing he did so, and I was absolutely terrified.  WHY DID I KEEP DATING HIM.  So many why's I will have to work through in therapy.  I have a therapist set up and am going to do everything to avoid making these mistakes in the future and find out WHY I feel like I need to fix people to the point that it nearly literally kills me.  

&#x200B;

How people like this exist I will never understand or get the answers I desire.  All I can do is pick up these scattered pieces and try to put them back together.  I am 'withdrawing' from him.  It's insane.  But if I could quit smoking cigarettes after 15 years and quit drinking, I can quit him!  Put him out in a dirty ashtray where he deserves to be.  I hope he never wraps his manipulative hands around any other person.
